[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=0.4]
\draw[gray!30,very thin,xstep=1,ystep=1] (0,0) grid (5,15);
\draw[->] (0,0)--(0,16);
\draw[->] (0,0)--(6,0);
\foreach \y in {3,6,9,12,15} {\node[left,font=\scriptsize] at (-0.3,\y) {$\y$};}
\node[below left,font=\scriptsize] at (0,0) {$0$};
\foreach \x in {1,2,3,4,5} {\node[below,font=\scriptsize] at (\x,0) {$\x$};}
\draw[very thick,blue] (0,0)--(5,15);
\foreach \pt in {(0,0),(5,15)} {\fill[blue] \pt circle (2.5pt);}
\node[rotate=90,font=\scriptsize] at (-1.6,7.5) {Speed (m/s)};
\node[below,font=\scriptsize] at (2.5,-1.2) {Time (s)};
\node[font=\scriptsize] at (2.5,16.6) {A cyclist accelerating from rest};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
A cyclist accelerates from rest at a constant rate, as shown. Find the acceleration, in m/s².

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=0.35]
\draw[gray!30,very thin,xstep=1,ystep=2] (0,0) grid (6,18);
\draw[->] (0,0)--(0,19.2);
\draw[->] (0,0)--(7,0);
\foreach \y in {2,4,6,8,10,12,14,16,18} {\node[left,font=\scriptsize] at (-0.3,\y) {$\y$};}
\node[below left,font=\scriptsize] at (0,0) {$0$};
\foreach \x in {1,2,3,4,5,6} {\node[below,font=\scriptsize] at (\x,0) {$\x$};}
\draw[very thick,blue] (0,18)--(6,0);
\foreach \pt in {(0,18),(6,0)} {\fill[blue] \pt circle (2.5pt);}
\node[rotate=90,font=\scriptsize] at (-1.6,9) {Speed (m/s)};
\node[below,font=\scriptsize] at (3,-1.2) {Time (s)};
\node[font=\scriptsize] at (3,19.8) {A bus braking to a stop};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
A bus decelerates at a constant rate until it comes to a complete stop, as shown. Find the magnitude of its deceleration, in m/s².

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=0.55]
\draw[gray!30,very thin,xstep=1,ystep=1] (0,0) grid (10,6);
\draw[->] (0,0)--(0,6.6);
\draw[->] (0,0)--(11,0);
\foreach \v/\p in {10/1,20/2,30/3,40/4,50/5,60/6} {\draw (-0.15,\p)--(0,\p); \node[left,font=\scriptsize] at (-0.15,\p) {$\v$};}
\node[below left,font=\scriptsize] at (0,0) {$0$};
\foreach \x in {2,4,6,8,10} {\node[below,font=\scriptsize] at (\x,0) {$\x$};}
\draw[very thick,blue] (2,2)--(10,6);
\fill[blue] (2,2) circle (2.5pt);
\fill[blue] (10,6) circle (2.5pt);
\node[rotate=90,font=\scriptsize] at (-1.5,3) {Speed (m/s)};
\node[below,font=\scriptsize] at (5,-1.2) {Time (s)};
\node[font=\scriptsize] at (5,6.6) {An aircraft accelerating for take-off};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
An aircraft is already rolling down the runway when its speed is first graphed, and it continues accelerating at a constant rate toward take-off, as shown. Find its acceleration, in m/s².

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=0.35]
\draw[gray!30,very thin,xstep=1,ystep=2] (0,0) grid (12,16);
\draw[->] (0,0)--(0,17.2);
\draw[->] (0,0)--(13,0);
\foreach \y in {2,4,6,8,10,12,14,16} {\node[left,font=\scriptsize] at (-0.3,\y) {$\y$};}
\node[below left,font=\scriptsize] at (0,0) {$0$};
\foreach \x in {4,9,12} {\node[below,font=\scriptsize] at (\x,0) {$\x$};}
\draw[very thick,blue] (0,0)--(4,16)--(9,16)--(12,0);
\foreach \pt in {(0,0),(4,16),(9,16),(12,0)} {\fill[blue] \pt circle (2.5pt);}
\node[rotate=90,font=\scriptsize] at (-1.6,8) {Speed (m/s)};
\node[below,font=\scriptsize] at (6,-1.2) {Time (s)};
\node[font=\scriptsize] at (6,17.8) {A motorbike's three-stage ride};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
A motorbike speeds up, then travels at a steady speed, then slows down, as shown. During which time interval is the motorbike's acceleration $0$?

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=0.33]
\draw[gray!30,very thin,xstep=1,ystep=2] (0,0) grid (13,16);
\draw[->] (0,0)--(0,17.2);
\draw[->] (0,0)--(14,0);
\foreach \y in {2,4,6,8,10,12,14,16} {\node[left,font=\scriptsize] at (-0.3,\y) {$\y$};}
\node[below left,font=\scriptsize] at (0,0) {$0$};
\foreach \x in {4,9,13} {\node[below,font=\scriptsize] at (\x,0) {$\x$};}
\draw[very thick,blue] (0,0)--(4,16)--(9,16)--(13,0);
\foreach \pt in {(0,0),(4,16),(9,16),(13,0)} {\fill[blue] \pt circle (2.5pt);}
\node[rotate=90,font=\scriptsize] at (-1.6,8) {Speed (m/s)};
\node[below,font=\scriptsize] at (6.5,-1.2) {Time (s)};
\node[font=\scriptsize] at (6.5,17.8) {A motorbike's three-stage ride};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
A motorbike speeds up, cruises, then brakes to a stop, as shown. Find its deceleration during the final stage (from $9$ to $13$ seconds), in m/s².

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=0.7]
\draw[gray!30,very thin,xstep=1,ystep=1] (0,0) grid (5,5);
\draw[->] (0,0)--(0,5.6);
\draw[->] (0,0)--(6,0);
\foreach \v/\p in {4/1,8/2,12/3,16/4,20/5} {\draw (-0.15,\p)--(0,\p); \node[left,font=\scriptsize] at (-0.15,\p) {$\v$};}
\node[below left,font=\scriptsize] at (0,0) {$0$};
\foreach \x in {1,2,3,4,5} {\node[below,font=\scriptsize] at (\x,0) {$\x$};}
\draw[very thick,blue] (0,5)--(5,0);
\draw[very thick,red] (0,5)--(4,0);
\foreach \pt in {(0,5),(5,0),(4,0)} {\fill[black] \pt circle (2.5pt);}
\node[font=\scriptsize,blue,below right] at (2.5,2.6) {Car M};
\node[font=\scriptsize,red,above left] at (1.6,2) {Car N};
\node[rotate=90,font=\scriptsize] at (-1.3,2.5) {Speed (m/s)};
\node[below,font=\scriptsize] at (2.5,-1.2) {Time (s)};
\node[font=\scriptsize] at (2.5,5.6) {Two cars braking to a stop};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
Two cars, both travelling at the same speed, brake to a stop at different constant rates, as shown. Which car decelerates more sharply, and by how much?

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=0.34]
\draw[gray!30,very thin,xstep=1,ystep=1] (0,0) grid (19,9);
\draw[->] (0,0)--(0,9.6);
\draw[->] (0,0)--(20,0);
\foreach \y in {1,2,3,4,5,6,7,8,9} {\node[left,font=\scriptsize] at (-0.3,\y) {$\y$};}
\node[below left,font=\scriptsize] at (0,0) {$0$};
\foreach \x in {4,10,12,16,19} {\node[below,font=\scriptsize] at (\x,0) {$\x$};}
\draw[very thick,blue] (0,0)--(4,8)--(10,8)--(12,0)--(16,0)--(19,9);
\foreach \pt in {(0,0),(4,8),(10,8),(12,0),(16,0),(19,9)} {\fill[blue] \pt circle (2.5pt);}
\node[rotate=90,font=\scriptsize] at (-1.6,4.5) {Speed (m/s)};
\node[below,font=\scriptsize] at (9.5,-1.2) {Time (s)};
\node[font=\scriptsize] at (9.5,10.2) {A lift travelling between floors};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
A lift speeds up, cruises, slows to a stop at a floor, waits with its doors open, then departs again, as shown. Find its acceleration as it departs, from $16$ seconds onward, in m/s².

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=0.32]
\draw[gray!30,very thin,xstep=1,ystep=2] (0,0) grid (9,20);
\draw[->] (0,0)--(0,21.2);
\draw[->] (0,0)--(10,0);
\foreach \y in {4,8,12,16,20} {\node[left,font=\scriptsize] at (-0.3,\y) {$\y$};}
\node[below left,font=\scriptsize] at (0,0) {$0$};
\foreach \x in {4,9} {\node[below,font=\scriptsize] at (\x,0) {$\x$};}
\draw[very thick,blue] (0,0)--(4,20)--(9,0);
\foreach \pt in {(0,0),(4,20),(9,0)} {\fill[blue] \pt circle (2.5pt);}
\node[rotate=90,font=\scriptsize] at (-1.8,10) {Speed (m/s)};
\node[below,font=\scriptsize] at (4.5,-1.2) {Time (s)};
\node[font=\scriptsize] at (4.5,21.8) {A delivery van};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
A delivery van accelerates hard, then brakes to a stop, as shown. Find the difference between the magnitudes of its acceleration and its deceleration, in m/s².
